# Valhalla routing engine. Server-side only.
#
# Note the missing VITE_ prefix: that is deliberate. Vite only inlines VITE_*
# variables into the client bundle, so these values never reach the browser.
# The browser talks to /api/isochrone, /api/route and /api/health, which the
# dev server (and the Cloudflare Worker in production) forwards to this
# Valhalla instance with the costing model, walking speed and Richmond-area
# bounds fixed server-side.
#
# Self-hosting (the intended setup) is documented in valhalla/README.md.
# Once the Compose stack is running AND you have applied that README's
# max_contours edit to data/valhalla.json:
#
#   VALHALLA_URL=http://localhost:8002
#   VALHALLA_MAX_CONTOURS=100
#
# VALHALLA_MAX_CONTOURS must match the instance's
# service_limits.isochrone.max_contours. The dial ladder is every minute from
# 5 to 100, so 96 contours: with 100 the whole ladder is a single upstream
# query. Against a stock instance (limit 4) leave it unset and the proxy
# splits the ladder into 24 chunks of 4. Setting it higher than the instance
# allows gets the whole batch rejected upstream. Anything that is not a
# positive integer falls back to the stock limit of 4.
#
# For evaluation only, FOSSGIS runs a public community instance. It is shared
# infrastructure, not a production dependency: fine for trying the app out,
# not something to leave under a public deployment.
#
#   VALHALLA_URL=https://valhalla1.openstreetmap.de
#   # leave VALHALLA_MAX_CONTOURS unset (stock limit of 4)
#
# Once either is running, `curl localhost:5173/api/health` answers whether
# the proxy can reach it, and which tileset it is serving.
#
# For production: `npx wrangler deploy` reads VALHALLA_URL from wrangler.toml
# [vars], or set it as a secret if the URL itself should stay private.
VALHALLA_URL=
VALHALLA_MAX_CONTOURS=

# The forecast upstream. Server-side only, same as the two above, and unset is
# fine: the proxy falls back to Open-Meteo. It exists so the vendor can be
# swapped without a code change - the proxy normalises the response into this
# app's own shape rather than forwarding it, so switching is one module.
#
# THE LICENCE. Open-Meteo's data is CC-BY 4.0 and its free API tier is sold as
# non-commercial use only: "The free API is for non-commercial use,
# rate-limited to 10,000 calls/day, and carries no uptime guarantee."
# Commercial use - their examples are "websites or apps that have subscriptions
# or display advertisements" - needs a paid plan and an API key. This build
# assumes the commercial case, which is why WEATHER_ENABLED in
# src/lib/weather.ts ships false: see docs/plans/HUMAN-REVIEW.md.
# https://api.weather.gov is the public-domain fallback the normalised response
# shape exists to permit, at the cost of two round trips, a required
# User-Agent, and no UV index.
WEATHER_URL=
